---
title: "Figure 7 — Operator Console: login, session, and role-based approval flow"
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Operator / Viewer
    participant B as Browser
    participant C as Console (Flask)
    participant US as UserStore<br/>(werkzeug hashes)
    participant Q as ApprovalQueue<br/>(shared with monitor)

    Note over U,C: 1 — Authentication
    U->>B: open console
    B->>C: GET /login
    C-->>B: login form
    U->>B: username + password
    B->>C: POST /login
    C->>US: verify(username, password)
    alt invalid
        US-->>C: None
        C-->>B: 401 — re-render with error
    else valid
        US-->>C: User(role)
        C-->>B: 302 → set signed session cookie {user, role}
    end

    Note over U,C: 2 — Every subsequent request
    B->>C: GET /dashboard | /approvals | /policy | /sequence | /audit
    C->>C: login_required — session has user?
    alt no session
        C-->>B: 302 → /login
    else authenticated
        C-->>B: 200 — rendered view (read-only observation)
    end

    Note over U,Q: 3 — Acting on a gate (role-gated)
    B->>C: POST /approvals/{id}/approve
    C->>C: requires_role(operator)
    alt viewer
        C-->>B: 403 — read-only role
    else operator
        C->>Q: resolve(approval_id, approved, operator)
        Q-->>C: PendingApproval(status)
        Note right of Q: unblocks the monitor's<br/>await_resolution; writes<br/>ApprovalResolutionEvent
        C-->>B: 302 → /approvals (flash result)
    end

    Note over U,C: 4 — Logout
    B->>C: GET /logout
    C-->>B: 302 → /login (session cleared)
